  "answer": "The account is **570284196633** (sandbox6217). It tops the cost monitor's September breakdown at $13,548.63, ahead of sandbox6230 (247819305566) at $11,204.66.\n\n**Who holds it now:** tnakashima (tnakashima@example.com), lab GUID w6hcx, envtype sbx-ocp-gitops, conan_status in_use.\n\n**When their lab was provisioned:** AAP2 has one job for w6hcx, provision job 84152 on `west`. It started 2026-09-18T14:51:07Z and succeeded at 15:38:22Z. There is no earlier job for that GUID.\n\n**What Cost Explorer shows (2026-09-01 to 2026-10-01, exclusive end):** $13,548.63 in total (EC2 compute $12,807.53, EC2 - Other $741.10). The daily series falls into two separate blocks:\n\n- 2026-09-01 to 2026-09-12: about $630-650/day of EC2 compute plus $38.50/day of EC2 - Other, tapering to $214.30 on 09-12. That block is **$7,718.43**.\n- 2026-09-13 to 2026-09-17: no charges at all.\n- 2026-09-18 to 2026-09-30: $96.40 + $6.10 on the provisioning day, then about $450-462/day plus $22.75/day. That block is **$5,830.20**.\n\n**Billing:**\n- Bill tnakashima **$5,830.20**, the spend from 2026-09-18, when their lab was provisioned, through 2026-09-30.\n- **$7,718.43** (2026-09-01 to 2026-09-12) should not go to them. It predates their lab by almost a week, and it ends with five days of zero spend before their provision. That is a previous tenant's usage. The sandbox DB and AAP2 only show the current holder, so these tools can't say who that tenant was. Their lab's destroy job, or the pool's assignment history, is where to look.\n\nApplying the month-end rule here would overcharge tnakashima by $7,718.43, more than half the bill.\n"
